course: dictionary
lesson: 9398
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word «sprite» is a good example. «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» The words costumes, pictures and animation show that a sprite here is a picture that moves on a screen.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «Many bugs are tiny... or a ghost effect that makes the sprite invisible», the words bugs, script and effect tell you we are talking about computer programs, not fairies.
explain: A capital letter is a clue too. «Sprite» with a capital S is a brand name for a lemon-lime fizzy drink. «Une limonade est fizzy lemonade, like Sprite» compares it to lemonade, so the clue is the drink.
fact: A sprite can mean a small magical creature, like a fairy or elf, in stories.
fact: In computing, a sprite is a small picture or character that moves around, such as the cat in Scratch.
fact: In science, a red sprite is a rare flash of red light high above a thunderstorm, photographed from planes and space.
fact: «Sprite» with a capital S is the name of a lemon-lime fizzy drink.
fact: Words with more than one meaning are called multiple-meaning words, and the context tells you which meaning is used.
exercise: «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» What is a sprite in this sentence? | A fizzy drink | *A small picture or character that moves on screen | A bolt of lightning from a storm | A tiny magical creature with wings
exercise: «Une limonade est fizzy lemonade, like Sprite.» What kind of thing is Sprite here? | A horse in a story | A type of thunderstorm | *A lemon-lime fizzy drink | A computer bug
exercise: «repeat 5: move 10, turn right 72» turns 5 × 72 = 360 degrees in all. How many degrees does the sprite turn in all? | 5 | *360 | 10 | 72
test: A sprite moves with «x = x + speed», where speed is 4 for 25 frames. Starting at x = 0, where does it end? | x = 25 | *x = 100 | x = 29 | x = 4
test: In stories, sprites are water or air spirits in myths and fairy tales. What is a sprite in a fairy tale? | A tiny mistake in a computer program | *A small magical creature, like a fairy or elf | A fizzy lemon-lime drink | A red flash of light over a storm
exam: Ella says «sprite» always means a fizzy drink. Why is she wrong? | Sprite is only a French word | Sprite always means a fizzy drink, so she is right | Sprite is a kind of storm | *Sprite also means a magical creature, a moving picture in a game and a science word, and only the capital-S Sprite is a drink
